(13, 'Flower Market Dadar', 'flower-market-dadar', '20230228050425c99554ab98b617033760542427d04ae8.jpg', 'JJ Mehta & Sons Camera Store', 1, '2025-11-29 07:00:00', 'Whether it is a bouquet of roses or a garland of marigolds, flowers tend to bring a smile to anyone’s face. Located in the hustling areas of the busiest city of Mumbai, there exists one such market that’s responsible for smiles on the thousands of its visitors. Known for its densely populated commercial and residential settlements, Dadar possesses a lane of flowers that is nothing but a figment of a fairy tale, except for its chaos. Situated near the Dadar railway station, this place is apparently a colorful paradise for flower lovers and photographers. We are talking about the Dadar Flower Market we are happy to  take you on a memorable experience that this market offers.', '20230228052443349ac207f3c82750f31bc044f9d36250.jpg', 'The market opens before the first rays of the sun embrace the ground. Commencing from 4 A.M. The energy around the market spikes gradually as the flowers from neighboring districts of Kolhapur, Satara, Sangli, etc, get imported. Though the market operates almost daily, the best opportunity for some bustling street photography is right when the market opens and this is exactly what our community, at Photo Walks India, strives for.', 'One experiences a spectacular audio-visual symphony formed through screams of buyers and sellers and bustling, immense bargaining, and especially the smiles of the customers. Vendors sell floral items such as bouquets, flower pots, garlands, and other decor accessories. The crowd gets way too overwhelming during the festive days', '20230228051534c68c1d83d9f9f55de43e65b04c3eb407.png', '. People from the corners of the city buy huge quantities of flowers for functions and events. The market’s indication of hospitality is its pleasant and overwhelming mixed fragrances of flowers, making it a treat for everyone’s eyes, especially photographers.', 'The humongous flower market is a hub for a variety of pretty and colorful flowers available at prices that you’ll hardly witness anywhere else. If you wish to buy bulk quantities of flowers wholesale, well, no other place can be better than this. Marigolds, roses, lilies, jasmines, tulips; you name it and you have it. Some flowers may be seasonable but the refreshing essence in the air around the market area is evergreen.', 'Every flower blossoms with a beautiful significance. You can feel the warmth in the saffron-colored marigolds, a loving embrace among the red roses, camaraderie among the jasmines, a peaceful radiance in the white lilies, prosperity in the leaves of tulsi, and Indian festive energy in the vermillion hues of garlands. These aren’t just the colors of flowers lying around in the baskets but the colors that represent the cultural diversity that one gets to witness in this country.', NULL, '20230228051534e05c1eb5e28d1f85c5b13d855ac912e4.png', 'Amid the incredible and vivid visuals of the market, the sunlight filtering through the petals and leaves of the flowers creates beautiful natural lighting for photographers to play with for capturing lively pictures. The colorful backdrop, vibrant energy, and most importantly, a varied range of subjects are nothing less than a dream venue for a photoshoot.', 'The Photo Walks India Community offers an excellent opportunity to capture effervescent photographs and hone your skills at various mesmerizing venues like the Dadar flower market. We believe that a camera’s lens has the potential to tell a million stories and we wish to give them a deserved chance to get told.', '202302280515350b682e1922783862856c02fb49c6f8ab.png', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '{\"1\":\"Note : If you are sharing a camera please get your SD we do not give photos back since they are demo products and photos will be formatted once the photowalk is over\",\"2\":\"Anyone interested in Photography and would like to spend morning weekends clicking and walking around the city\",\"3\":\"Like to meet and interact with photography enthusiast and would love to join our photowalk community\",\"4\":\"If you do not have a camera we will provide you with a mirrorless camera that will be shared with other participants during the photowalk. Please carry a SD Card to so you can take your clicked photos back. We would require a photo ID with address proof to be submitted at the time of the photowalk.\",\"5\":\"Please note that photo walks are done on foot, so expect lots of walking.\",\"6\":\"Photowalk is open to all above the Age of 18 Years\"}', '<iframe src=\"https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d3148.2403521103006!2d72.83980577425028!3d19.01995605373147!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x3be7cedb0b692529%3A0xc30f9e5bb7df4d8d!2sJ%20J%20Mehta%20and%20Sons!5e1!3m2!1sen!2sin!4v1763780831060!5m2!1sen!2sin\" width=\"100%\" height=\"650\" style=\"border:0;\" allowfullscreen=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer-when-downgrade\"></iframe>', 1, 'https://fujifilmxacademy.com/activity/capturing-petal-at-dadar-flower-market/6911b875e7576e78b7300013', 'photowalkdadar, flowermarker, photowalkindia', 'photowalkdadar, flowermarker, photowalkindia', '2023-02-28 12:04:28', '2025-11-22 10:07:48', NULL),
(14, 'Villages of Bandra', 'villages-of-bandra', '20230411053752afc24b07d77918c7851b4fb19b2f138c.png', 'Joggers Park Bandra', 1, '2025-03-08 07:30:00', 'Chimbai and Ranwar are two beautiful neighborhoods situated in Bandra, Mumbai. These two villages will make you experience the old charm of Mumbai. Located in the heart of Bandra, Chibai is a small fishing village. It is well known for its busy fish markets, narrow streets, and vibrant auras. The colorful houses and the murals on the street amplify the beauty of this place. Explore these amazing locations, create memories, and capture the photos for an experience to last a lifetime.', '2023041105170316e768d8d1c8696119106e0a08f4b7d6.jpg', 'In the hustle and bustle of Mumbai commercial city, finding yourself in tranquil and serene locations is surely a miracle. The villages in Bandra are surely such places. Places where peace grows through its amazing people and its picturesque sceneries.', 'Today, at Photo Walks India, we will introduce you to one such amazing location where history, culture, and charming works of architecture have made a home. Come join us as we discover the beauty of these places like never before.', '20230411052514fdd7a505e22a0c40c63f361e9a3ff10e.png', 'Chimbai and Ranwar are two beautiful neighborhoods situated in Bandra, Mumbai. These two villages will make you experience the old charm of Mumbai. Located in the heart of Bandra, Chibai is a small fishing village', 'It is well known for its busy fish markets, narrow streets, and vibrant auras. The colorful houses and the murals on the street amplify the beauty of this place. Explore these amazing locations, create memories, and capture the photos for an experience to last a lifetime.', 'Photo Walks India offers photographers an opportunity to capture the vibrant colors and the unique street art that decorate the walls of this village. Capture amazing candids of locals as they carry on with their lives in the bustling fish market.', 'The astonishing Bandra-worli sea link adds to the beauty of these breathtaking landscapes and sceneries. This place is definitely a heaven for street photographers out there.', '20230411053528b98645ae8fac0b33f6bcae4fe6a22aa2.png', 'Moving ahead with your journey to the Ranwar Village- The old bungalows lining the narrow roads of this pretty neighborhood is a sight worth capturing with your lenses. With each building telling its own tale, this place has become a photographer’s paradise. Ranwar offers you endless photographic opportunities, from landscapes to candids, you can capture them all!', 'These villages also have some of the oldest temples and churches with significant cultural importance. The intricate details, bungalows\' colorful frontages, and friendly locals\' warm hospitality will allow you to capture some of the most fantastic portraits and landscapes. The amazing personalities and lifestyles of the locals are a treat for inspiration-searching photographers.If you want to add a layer of richness to your photographic experience, come together with Photo Walks India and get a glimpse of these two hidden gems of India, the Chimbai and Ranwar villages - where beauty flows and culture resides.', '202304110531065887bd7b3a8a7d2b645e9a10f96d22f2.png', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '{\"1\":\"Photowalk is open to all above the Age of 18 Years\",\"2\":\"Anyone interested in Photography and would like to spend morning weekends clicking and walking around the city\",\"3\":\"Like to meet and interact with photography enthusiast and would love to join our photowalk community\",\"4\":\"If you do not have a camera we will provide you with a mirrorless camera that will be shared with other participants during the photowalk. Please carry a SD Card to so you can take your clicked photos back. We would require a photo ID with address proof to be submitted at the time of the photowalk.\",\"5\":\"Please note that photo walks are done on foot, so expect lots of walking.\",\"6\":\"Note : If you are sharing a camera please get your SD we do not give photos back since they are demo products and photos will be formatted once the photowalk is over\"}', '<iframe src=\"https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d30168.76478590411!2d72.78844381562499!3d19.059534!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x3be7c96982a43755%3A0xfc1fb95ad1eb5bcc!2sJoggers%20Park!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sin!4v1681187757285!5m2!1sen!2sin\" width=\"100%\" height=\"450\" style=\"border:0;\" allowfullscreen=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer-when-downgrade\"></iframe>', 1, NULL, 'photowalk bandra villages', 'vilalge of bandra photowalk', '2023-04-11 11:37:28', '2025-03-02 21:24:54', NULL),
(15, 'Banganga', 'banganga', '20230421195554bd15001d2407ad0fe3537986b4001b5a.jpg', 'Legend Super Bazaar', 1, '2023-05-13 07:30:00', 'Banganga Tank offers a timeless destination for photographers seeking to capture the essence of this spiritual oasis. This ancient water tank, steeped in history and cultural significance, provides a plethora of opportunities for an enchanting and immersive photo walk. As you embark on your photographic journey with Photowalk India at Banganga Tank, you are transported to a realm of architectural splendor. The intricately carved stone steps, adorned with sculptures and motifs, speak to the extraordinary craftsmanship of artisans from bygone eras. The fusion of Hindu and Islamic architectural styles creates a captivating interplay of lines, curves, and patterns, reflecting the diverse cultural influences that have shaped Mumbai\'s past.', '20230421200525d3e54829159ba1d41fc52ef02ebfb6c1.jpg', 'In the bustling metropolis of Mumbai, amidst the skyscrapers, busy streets, and cacophony of urban life, lies a serene oasis of spirituality - the Banganga Tank. This ancient water tank, nestled in the heart of the city, holds deep religious significance and is a place where history, culture, and faith come together.', 'Banganga Tank offers a timeless destination for photographers seeking to capture the essence of this spiritual oasis. This ancient water tank, steeped in history and cultural significance, provides a plethora of opportunities for an enchanting and immersive photo walk. As you embark on your photographic journey with Photowalk India at Banganga Tank, you are transported to a realm of architectural splendor.', '2023042119555432f67985cad3d625a694c09415422e2d.png', 'The intricately carved stone steps, adorned with sculptures and motifs, speak to the extraordinary craftsmanship of artisans from bygone eras. The fusion of Hindu and Islamic architectural styles creates a captivating interplay of lines, curves, and patterns, reflecting the diverse cultural influences that have shaped Mumbai\'s past.', 'The Banganga Tank, also known as Banganga Stepwell, is a rectangular-shaped water reservoir that spans over 2,500 square meters. It is believed to have been built during the 12th century by the Silhara dynasty, a Hindu dynasty that ruled the region at that time', 'The tank was constructed to provide a perennial source of freshwater for the residents of the Walkeshwar Temple complex, which is located adjacent to the tank. The play of light and shadows on the weathered stone steps, the reflections on the water\'s surface, and the intricate details of the carvings offer a treasure trove of captivating subjects for your lens. The serene and tranquil atmosphere of the tank, amidst the hustle and bustle of Mumbai, adds a touch of mystique to your photographs, creating an otherworldly ambiance that is sure to captivate the viewer.', 'The tank complex is also adorned with small shrines and temples dedicated to various Hindu deities. These colorful and intricately adorned shrines offer excellent opportunities for close-up shots of the intricate craftsmanship, vibrant decorations, and the devout locals offering prayers. The juxtaposition of faith, tradition, and artistry makes for compelling photographic subjects that capture the soul of Mumbai\'s diverse culture.', '2023042119555463c009a2a19fd608150a7c992990807a.png', 'Despite being located in the heart of a bustling city, the Banganga Tank exudes a sense of tranquility and calmness. The serene environment, the soothing sound of water, and the majestic architecture make it a perfect place for introspection, meditation, and connecting with the divine. Many locals and tourists visit the tank to seek solace, offer prayers, and experience the spiritual energy that permeates the air.', 'In conclusion, we at Photowalks India are all set to take you on a journey through Mumbai\'s spiritual oasis, offering a captivating and immersive experience into the city\'s history, culture, and architectural marvels. With its mesmerizing beauty, serenity, and cultural significance, Banganga Tank is a photographer\'s paradise, where every corner tells a story and every click of the shutter captures a piece of Mumbai\'s soul.', '20230421195555c909dea51ecbd2a40abd82dde6c2ce89.png', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '[\"Photowalk is open to all above the Age of 18 Years\",\"Anyone interested in Photography and would like to spend morning weekends clicking and walking around the city\",\"Like to meet and interact with photography enthusiast and would love to join our photowalk community\",\"If you do not have a camera we will provide you with a mirrorless camera that will be shared with other participants during the photowalk. Please carry a SD Card to so you can take your clicked photos back. We would require a photo ID with address proof to be submitted at the time of the photowalk.\",\"Please note that photo walks are done on foot, so expect lots of walking.\",\"Note : If you are sharing a camera please get your SD we do not give photos back since they are demo products and photos will be formatted once the photowalk is over\"]', '<iframe src=\"https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d1886.8363989564266!2d72.79390089291807!3d18.94587175275049!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x3be7cdfbcb68b677%3A0xae05bbb4a8c98f97!2sLegend%20Super%20Bazaar!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sin!4v1682106898382!5m2!1sen!2sin\" width=\"100%\" height=\"450\" style=\"border:0;\" allowfullscreen=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer-when-downgrade\"></iframe>', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2023-04-22 02:55:56', '2023-04-26 15:37:54', NULL),
(16, 'Flower Market Yard', 'flower-market-yard', '20230604171936cb3c24188807b526ebd13677ae0fbf8a.jpg', 'Puranchand & Sons Trading', 3, '2023-06-10 07:15:00', 'We at Photowalk India welcome you to an enchanting photowalk through the vibrant Market Yard Flower Market, nestled in the heart of Shivneri Peth, Pune. Join us as we immerse ourselves in a kaleidoscope of colors, capture intoxicating fragrances, and witness the bustling energy that fills the air of this captivating market.', '20230604173229e286c3f72d79d7492cbed080e4ab1fd1.png', 'We at Photowalk India welcome you to an enchanting photowalk through the vibrant Market Yard Flower Market, nestled in the heart of Shivneri Peth, Pune. Join us as we immerse ourselves in a kaleidoscope of colors, capture intoxicating fragrances, and witness the bustling energy that fills the air of this captivating market.', 'As the sun gently rises, casting a soft glow on the streets, we step into the Market Yard Flower Market with cameras in hand, ready to embark on a visual adventure. The market awakens, and our senses are immediately captivated by the vibrant tapestry of colors that unfolds before us.', '202306041719365b3a726054ff2f1eb653ba1388e4a669.png', 'As we venture deeper into the market, we are greeted by an extraordinary sight. Rows of flower stalls stretch as far as the eye can see, each adorned with a breathtaking array of blooms. Delicate roses in shades of pink, red, and white showcase their velvety petals, while vibrant marigolds exude an aura of warmth and joy. Our cameras click in rhythm with our excitement, capturing the essence of each flower in all its splendor.', 'The market is alive with activity, a symphony of sounds and fragrances that envelop us. Vendors meticulously arrange their flowers, skillfully weaving garlands of marigolds and jasmine that exude a captivating scent, enchanting our senses. We position ourselves to capture the intricate details, the delicate curves, and the interplay of light and shadow that make each flower a work of art.', 'As we meander through the market, our lenses are drawn to the exotic orchids, whose vibrant hues and intricate patterns leave us in awe. These stunning blooms seem to tell stories of far-off lands, of mystical forests and hidden treasures. We focus on capturing their ethereal beauty, highlighting the delicate veins on their petals and the enchanting color gradients that make each orchid a unique masterpiece.', 'Beyond the visual feast, we are captivated by the vibrant atmosphere and the human interactions that bring the market to life. Florists passionately arrange bouquets, their weathered hands showcasing years of experience and love for their craft. Customers browse the stalls, their eyes filled with wonder and anticipation, as they select the perfect blooms for their special occasions. We train our lenses on these fleeting moments, immortalizing the emotions and connections that blossom within this bustling marketplace.', '20230604172535cff2415b16d48a174d2a0103c3060ddd.png', 'As our photowalk nears its end, we take a moment to reflect on the beauty captured through our lenses. Each photograph tells a story, preserving the magic of Market Yard Flower Market in a single frame. The vivid colors, intoxicating fragrances, and bustling energy come alive, inviting viewers to experience the market\'s allure.So, grab your camera and embark on your own photowalk through the Market Yard Flower Market. Immerse yourself in the sea of colors, inhale the fragrant symphony, and let the vibrant energy ignite your creativity. With each click of the shutter, uncover the hidden gems, the captivating details, and the human stories that weave together to create the tapestry of Market Yard Flower Market in Shivneri Peth, Pune with Photowalk India.', 'Photocredits\r\n@yehpakkapitega \r\n@snapwithrushi', '202306041728396a9ee4b1902ade527072c8a59eacca13.png', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '{\"1\":\"Photowalk is open to all above the Age of 18 Years\",\"2\":\"Anyone interested in Photography and would like to spend morning weekends clicking and walking around the city\",\"3\":\"Like to meet and interact with photography enthusiast and would love to join our photowalk community\",\"4\":\"If you do not have a camera we will provide you with a mirrorless camera that will be shared with other participants during the photowalk. Please carry a SD Card to so you can take your clicked photos back. We would require a photo ID with address proof to be submitted at the time of the photowalk.\",\"5\":\"Please note that photo walks are done on foot, so expect lots of walking.\",\"6\":\"Note : If you are sharing a camera please get your SD we do not give photos back since they are demo products and photos will be formatted once the photowalk is over\"}', '<iframe src=\"https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d60535.71515316873!2d73.83968598082532!3d18.50709945095016!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x3bc2c1e3e877266d%3A0xe8d3b51be4875ab7!2sPuranchand%20and%20sons%20trading%20llp!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sin!4v1685900666257!5m2!1sen!2sin\" width=\"100%\" height=\"450\" style=\"border:0;\" allowfullscreen=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer-when-downgrade\"></iframe>', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2023-06-05 00:19:36', '2023-06-07 14:47:43', '2023-06-07 14:47:43'),
(17, 'Chor Bazaar', 'chor-bazaar', '202311281652097d71891bc8a6f6bb8620b04a67806d61.jpg', 'Shalimar Restaurant', 1, '2023-12-16 07:30:00', 'Photowalks India invites you to come with us on a visual journey through the narrow lanes and bustling alleys of Chor Bazaar, capturing the essence of this historical gem.\r\nChor Bazaar, meaning \'Thieves Market,\' has a rich history dating back to the mid-19th century during British colonial rule. Legend has it that the market earned its name due to the \"shor\" (noise) created by the alleged stolen goods that found their way here.  Photowalk attendees will have the chance to capture the vibrant chaos of the market, where the old seamlessly blends with the new. Antique furniture, classic gramophones, and quirky curiosities beckon photographers to immortalize the unique character of Chor Bazaar through their lenses.', '2023112816520918bf3fb640d0b37ddaf304aeca91b56f.png', 'In the heart of Mumbai, between all the hustle and bustle of the city, lies an iconic treasure trove of history and culture - Chor Bazaar. This vibrant market, known for its eclectic mix of antiques, vintage items, and unique finds, is a photographer\'s paradise waiting to be explored. Photowalks India invites you to come with us on a visual journey through the narrow lanes and bustling alleys of Chor Bazaar, capturing the essence of this historical gem.', 'Chor Bazaar, meaning \'Thieves Market,\' has a rich history dating back to the mid-19th century during British colonial rule. Legend has it that the market earned its name due to the \"shor\" (noise) created by the alleged stolen goods that found their way here. Over the years, the market has transformed into a labyrinthine treasure trove, attracting locals and tourists alike with its diverse array of artifacts.', '20231128165209c915bc77db48082fba81289c72f9dea9.png', 'As you stroll through the maze-like lanes, your lens will capture glimpses of the past embedded in the architecture and artifacts. From vintage Bollywood posters to ancient timepieces, Chor Bazaar stands as a living museum, each item narrating a tale of its own. Photowalk participants will have the opportunity to freeze these stories in time, creating a visual tapestry of Mumbai\'s bygone eras.', 'Chor Bazaar is a in itself is a mix of kaleidoscopic colors, textures, and cultures. Photowalk attendees will have the chance to capture the vibrant chaos of the market, where the old seamlessly blends with the new. Antique furniture, classic gramophones, and quirky curiosities beckon photographers to immortalize the unique character of Chor Bazaar through their lenses.', 'Among all the items on display, one might stumble upon rare coins, vintage cameras, and intricate Persian carpets. The market\'s charm lies in its unpredictability – you never know what hidden gems you might uncover. Photowalks India provides the perfect opportunity to document the diversity of Chor Bazaar, from its crowded stalls to the hidden corners that unveil the true spirit of this cultural melting pot.', 'While all the antiques consciously gain your attention something that shouldn’t be neglected is the heartbeat of Chor Bazaar; is its people, each with a story etched on their faces. You will have the privilege of capturing candid moments with the market\'s friendly vendors, who bring the market to life with their stories and experiences. From seasoned antique dealers to young artisans crafting unique pieces, the faces of Chor Bazaar reflect the spirit of resilience and passion that defines this historic market.', '202311281652106250148ea2781d9444a3fc8b47a2100e.png', 'As your lens captures the expressions of those who call Chor Bazaar home, you\'ll find a deeper connection to the heart of Mumbai.', 'Photowalks India encourages participants to engage with the locals, learn about their crafts, and share in the vibrant energy that permeates the air.', '20231128165211b66748ea3e0c37c8e453a7e39bc4bc11.png', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '[\"Photowalk is open to all above the Age of 18 Years\",\"Get to meet and interact with photography enthusiast and would love to join our photowalk community\",\"Anyone interested in Photography and would like to spend morning weekends clicking and walking around the city\",\"If you do not have a camera we will provide you with a mirrorless camera that will be shared with other participants during the photowalk. Please carry a SD Card to so you can take your clicked photos back. We would require a photo ID with address proof to be submitted at the time of the photowalk.\",\"Please note that photo walks are done on foot, so expect lots of walking.\"]', '<iframe src=\"https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d3773.398388404219!2d72.82974717437877!3d18.958005255667796!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x3be7ce3c58d7bbeb%3A0xd5367b7032593948!2sShalimar%20Restaurant!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sin!4v1701188217570!5m2!1sen!2sin\" width=\"100%\" height=\"450\" style=\"border:0;\" allowfullscreen=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer-when-downgrade\"></iframe>', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2023-11-28 23:52:11', '2023-11-29 11:10:08', NULL),
(18, 'Marina Beach', 'marina-beach', '202312021752445e003da451dd7e318437e28ac48609e1.jpg', 'Marina Light House', 7, '2026-01-31 06:00:00', 'Marina Beach, an iconic stretch along the Bay of Bengal, a shoreline with its living canvas that tells tales of history, culture, and everyday life in Chennai. As Photowalks India announces its upcoming event at Marina Beach, let\'s delve into the layers of this captivating location.\r\nMarina Beach was once a simple fishing village, and its transformation into the sprawling urban beach we see today is a testament to the city\'s evolution. The beach, originally named Madras Beach, played a crucial role in the city\'s trade activities during the colonial era.', '20231202175244b5c28f4472ee8cb2e6f3d1fecf2a9036.jpg', 'Marina Beach, an iconic stretch along the Bay of Bengal, a shoreline with its living canvas that tells tales of history, culture, and everyday life in Chennai. As Photowalks India announces its upcoming event at Marina Beach, let\'s delve into the layers of this captivating location.\r\nMarina Beach was once a simple fishing village, and its transformation into the sprawling urban beach we see today is a testament to the city\'s evolution. The beach, originally named Madras Beach, played a crucial role in the city\'s trade activities during the colonial era.', 'Marina Beach isn\'t merely a picturesque location; it\'s the beating heart of Chennai. It serves as a recreational space for families, a fitness ground for morning joggers, and a respite for those seeking solace in the rhythmic waves. Document the diverse activities and emotions that unfold against the backdrop of the sea; each frame captures a slice of Chennai\'s soul.\r\nAs we go about our photowalk, consider a few essential tips. Embrace the golden hours for enchanting natural light, be mindful of the ever-changing weather, and experiment with angles to add depth to your compositions. Capture candid moments of locals engaging with the beach – these shots often tell the most compelling stories.', '20231202182117dce7a8ffbf344abb70fc8356ea05161b.jpg', 'Over time, it evolved into a recreational hub, becoming the beloved Marina Beach we cherish today. \r\nAs you navigate the golden sands of Marina, you\'ll encounter architectural gems that punctuate the landscape. The Senate House, built in the Indo-Saracenic style, and the iconic Triumph of Labour statue stand as silent witnesses to the city\'s rich history.', 'Take a moment to absorb these structures, each echoing tales of Chennai\'s past. While talking about the history of Marina beach, one cannot experience Marina Beach fully without immersing in the lively atmosphere created by its vendors. From street food stalls offering crispy sundal to artists capturing the essence of the beach on canvas, these vendors contribute to the vibrancy of Marina.', 'Also, while chasing the perfect shot, remember to respect the privacy and sentiments of the locals. Seek permission before photographing individuals, especially in close-ups, and be conscious of cultural nuances.', 'Marina Beach is a shared space, and as photographers, we play a role in preserving its sanctity.', '2023120218032850a291082cab99a94030e6ef23d8ca84.png', 'These stalls, these vendors are somewhere adding life to the beach. The rhythmic chaos, a distinct style each one has to sell their goodies, the activities adds alot character to your photography. \r\nAs the vendors have been here for a longer time, when you interact with them, it is like a time machine has eloped in front of you to offer you with great stories.', 'What makes Street style photography complete is somewhat the power to dig out those untold stories out of your character and capture them in your memory forever!. Here at Marina, the stories are everywhere, they are standing beside you, waving at you, hiding from you, trying to find you; all you have to do is to step in! \r\nA protip here has to be that,  don\'t hesitate to interact with the locals; their stories might just add a unique perspective to your photo essay. In conclusion, Marina Beach is more than a picturesque setting for a photowalk – it\'s a living mosaic that reflects the soul of Chennai. So, gear up, embrace the sea breeze, and let your lens capture the myriad stories that unfold along the shores of Marina Beach. Happy shooting!', '20231202182117f679876d19688147030574013eea032a.png', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '{\"1\":\"Photowalk is open to all above the Age of 18 Years\",\"2\":\"Get to meet and interact with photography enthusiast and would love to join our photowalk community\",\"3\":\"Anyone interested in Photography and would like to spend morning weekends clicking and walking around the city\",\"4\":\"If you do not have a camera we will provide you with a mirrorless camera that will be shared with other participants during the photowalk. Please carry a SD Card to so you can take your clicked photos back. We would require a photo ID with address proof to be submitted at the time of the photowalk.\",\"5\":\"Please note that photo walks are done on foot, so expect lots of walking.\"}', '<iframe src=\"https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d3244.17451548519!2d80.27468497066299!3d13.039740585297611!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x3a526880556ddae5%3A0x5c17bd7aecfd0209!2sChennai%20Lighthouse!5e1!3m2!1sen!2sin!4v1769257964467!5m2!1sen!2sin\" width=\"100%\" height=\"650\" style=\"border:0;\" allowfullscreen=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer-when-downgrade\"></iframe>', 1, 'https://fujifilmxacademy.com/activity/golden-hour-walk-with-fujifilm/695b6a8600239d19067c1785', 'Marina Beach', 'Marina Beach, an iconic stretch along the Bay of Bengal, a shoreline with its living canvas that tells tales of history, culture, and everyday life in Chennai.', '2023-12-03 00:52:44', '2026-01-24 19:33:28', NULL),
(19, 'Mandai', 'mandai', '20231204135433e891223e6b8c046e8a77c11dd91dccd0.png', 'Digital Fantasy Store', 3, '2025-11-29 07:00:00', 'Mandai Phule Market, standing proudly since the 19th century, is a testament to Pune\'s endurance through the ages. Initially established during the British Raj, the market has not only stood the test of time but has flourished into one of the largest and economically significant markets in the city. Its architectural grandeur echoes the tales of a bygone era, whispering stories of traders, farmers, and artisans who have contributed to its legacy.', '20231204135433cfa43b47ed73383ed39e9e80650200e0.png', 'Pune, a city steeped in history and culture, has always been a canvas of vibrant stories waiting to be captured. As the cultural capital of Maharashtra, this bustling metropolis is not only known for its educational institutions and IT hubs but also for its rich heritage and the myriad experiences it offers. In the heart of Pune lies the Mandai Phule Market, a kaleidoscope of colors, aromas, and stories waiting to be unveiled. Photowalk India is thrilled to announce its next photowalk in this iconic marketplace, where every frame tells a tale of tradition, commerce, and resilience.', 'Before delving into the vibrant chaos of Mandai Phule Market, let\'s take a stroll down the historical lanes of Pune. Once the bastion of the Maratha Empire, Pune has evolved into a melting pot of tradition and modernity. The city\'s historical curtain is woven with threads of the Peshwa era, British colonial influence, and the contemporary vibrancy that defines it today.', '20231204141151a1ca04c2f2ce5516508b4ca486435365.png', 'Mandai Phule Market, standing proudly since the 19th century, is a testament to Pune\'s endurance through the ages. Initially established during the British Raj, the market has not only stood the test of time but has flourished into one of the largest and economically significant markets in the city. Its architectural grandeur echoes the tales of a bygone era, whispering stories of traders, farmers, and artisans who have contributed to its legacy.', 'Beyond the historical façade lies the economic heartbeat of Mandai Phule Market. Renowned as one of Pune\'s largest revenue-generating markets, it plays a pivotal role in the city\'s economic landscape. The market, a bustling hive of activity, hosts a myriad of vendors selling everything from fresh produce to spices, textiles, and local artifacts. The economic pulse of Mandai Phule Market beats strongly, reflecting the diverse canvas of commerce that defines Pune\'s cultural ethos.', 'The building itself, an architectural gem with its colonial charm, stands as a silent spectator to the changing tides of time. The intricate designs and arches are not just bricks and mortar but a living testament to the resilience of Pune\'s heritage. As photographers, this market is a canvas waiting to be painted with the hues of tradition, commerce, and human connection.', 'From the aromatic spices that have been a staple of Maharashtra\'s cuisine for centuries to the vibrant textiles that mirror the kaleidoscope of Indian traditions, every vendor contributes to the vibrant mosaic that is Mandai Phule Market.', '20231204135434a2ffc9686d47e8c7a2aa95acb9802d14.png', 'The vendors, with their weathered hands and warm smiles, are the real architects of Mandai Phule Market\'s charm. Each stall tells a story of hard work, passion, and a commitment to preserving the cultural heritage embedded in every product they offer.', 'As Photowalk India prepares to follow on this visual journey through Mandai Phule Market, we invite you to join us in capturing the spirit of Pune\'s cultural kaleidoscope. From the historical contours of Pune city to the bustling energy of Mandai Phule Market, every frame tells a story waiting to be heard. Let your lens be the storyteller as we unravel the layers of tradition, commerce, and community in this vibrant corner of Pune\'s beating heart.', '2023120414115153a65b16a22ee9fb93ae42c647b41974.png', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '{\"1\":\"Photowalk is open to all above the Age of 18 Years\",\"2\":\"Get to meet and interact with photography enthusiast and would love to join our photowalk community\",\"3\":\"Anyone interested in Photography and would like to spend morning weekends clicking and walking around the city\",\"4\":\"If you do not have a camera we will provide you with a mirrorless camera that will be shared with other participants during the photowalk. Please carry a SD Card to so you can take your clicked photos back. We would require a photo ID with address proof to be submitted at the time of the photowalk.\",\"5\":\"Please note that photo walks are done on foot, so expect lots of walking.\"}', '<iframe src=\"https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m14!1m8!1m3!1d15133.447152473636!2d73.8542016!3d18.5125461!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x3bc2c06d5f9aa37d%3A0x389ab6d4834c4c98!2sGoPro%20official%20Store%20(Digital%20Fantasy)!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sin!4v1701696264606!5m2!1sen!2sin\" width=\"100%\" height=\"450\" style=\"border:0;\" allowfullscreen=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer-when-downgrade\"></iframe>', 1, 'https://fujifilmxacademy.com/activity/punes-rangin-mandai/6911ba77e7576e78b7301663', 'photowalkspune, mandaiphotowalk,', 'photowalk at mandai', '2023-12-04 20:54:35', '2025-11-22 10:26:05', NULL),
(20, 'Fort Kochi', 'fort-kochi', '20231211171817b8c7100a4dc8493d46a10eb63133bb29.jpg', 'Opposite No 18 hotel', 10, '2025-12-27 06:30:00', 'As you step into the cobbled streets of Fort Kochi, you\'re not just visiting a location; you\'re stepping into a living history book. This picturesque town boasts a myriad of attractions, and one cannot miss the awe-inspiring Santa Cruz Basilica. The intricate architecture and serene ambiance of this church make it a must-capture spot for any photographer', '2023121117181738e89cca1bb916e2a69bd9dc6bbcf4e0.jpg', 'It\'s that time again – Photowalk India is back with another exciting adventure, and this time we\'re taking our lenses to the enchanting Fort Kochi in the heart of Kerala.', 'Nestled in the western part of Kochi city, this place is a treasure trove of history, culture, and visual delights. So, gear up, charge your cameras, and get ready to embark on a photographic journey like never before!', '20231211171817437175ab3904b8b1eb8838d474d66848.png', 'A Glimpse into Fort Kochi\'s Rich Heritage\r\nAs you step into the cobbled streets of Fort Kochi, you\'re not just visiting a location; you\'re stepping into a living history book. This picturesque town boasts a myriad of attractions, and one cannot miss the awe-inspiring Santa Cruz Basilica.', 'The intricate architecture and serene ambiance of this church make it a must-capture spot for any photographer.', 'History buffs, this one\'s for you! Fort Kochi is home to St. Francis Church, the very place where the legendary explorer Vasco da Gama was initially laid to rest. The centuries-old Dutch Seminary, the iconic China Vela, and various other historical monuments paint a vivid picture of the town\'s colonial past.', 'As you roam through the streets, you\'ll find yourself surrounded by the whispers of a bygone era, a melody that only history enthusiasts can truly appreciate.', '20231211171817370a54b5f6f01a309ddbc60c4f97b78c.png', 'Adding a touch of modernity to the historical landscape, Fort Kochi is also home to the Indian Navy\'s ship, Dronacharya. Imagine the striking contrast of this mighty vessel against the backdrop of ancient architecture – a juxtaposition that photographers dream of capturing. It\'s a sight that tells the tale of India\'s rich maritime history, from the past to the present.\r\n\r\nBut Fort Kochi isn\'t just about monuments and structures; it\'s about the people who call this place home. The residents of Fort Kochi, with their diverse cultural roots, add a vibrant tapestry to the town\'s landscape. From the bustling shops that line the streets to the charming locals you\'ll encounter, each frame tells a unique story of a community deeply connected to its heritage.\r\n\r\nThe old Portuguese buildings that line the streets are a testament to the town\'s colonial history. As you wander through the narrow lanes, you\'ll find yourself surrounded by a kaleidoscope of colors, textures, and architectural wonders. Every turn presents a new opportunity to capture the essence of a town that has gracefully preserved its past while embracing the present.', 'Why Fort Kochi? What Photographers Can Feel\r\nFor photographers, Fort Kochi is a canvas waiting to be painted with light and shadow. The blend of cultural richness, historical significance, and everyday life creates a unique atmosphere that\'s both inspiring and challenging. The interplay of tradition and modernity, the vivid palette of colors, and the intricate details in every nook and cranny make Fort Kochi a haven for those seeking to freeze moments in time.\r\n\r\nSo, fellow photography enthusiasts, mark your calendars and join us for an unforgettable Photowalk in Fort Kochi. Let\'s capture the soul of this town and create visual stories that will transport anyone who lays eyes on our photographs to the mesmerizing streets of Fort Kochi.\r\n\r\nSee you there, camera in hand, ready to unravel the tales of this cultural gem!', '20231211171818ded6c2949324f9816519f92b1508adf6.png', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '{\"1\":\"Photowalk is open to all above the Age of 18 Years\",\"2\":\"Get to meet and interact with photography enthusiast and would love to join our photowalk community\",\"3\":\"Anyone interested in Photography and would like to spend morning weekends clicking and walking around the city\",\"4\":\"If you do not have a camera we will provide you with a mirrorless camera that will be shared with other participants during the photowalk. Please carry a SD Card to so you can take your clicked photos back. We would require a photo ID with address proof to be submitted at the time of the photowalk.\",\"5\":\"Please note that photo walks are done on foot, so expect lots of walking.\"}', '<iframe width=\"100%\" height=\"650px\" frameborder=\"0\" style=\"border:0\" src=\"https://www.google.com/maps/embed/v1/place?key=AIzaSyB2NIWI3Tv9iDPrlnowr_0ZqZWoAQydKJU&q=No.%2018%20Hotel%2C%20KB%20Jacob%20Road%2C%20opposite%20Police%20Station%2C%20Fort%20Nagar%2C%20Near%2C%20Fort%20Kochi%2C%20Kochi%2C%20Kerala%2C%20India&maptype=roadmap\" allowfullscreen></iframe>', 1, 'https://fujifilmxacademy.com/activity/frame-the-heritage-fujifilm-photo-walk-at-fort-kochi/6936b27f05c494016b85cbfe', 'Fort Kochi Photowalk', 'Fort kochi photowalk', '2023-12-12 00:18:19', '2025-12-22 13:57:43', NULL),
(21, 'Qutub Minar', 'qutub-minar', '20231226080649a28f753c4e9cf2e0e00cc8336987236f.jpg', 'Qutub Minar Ticket Counter', 5, '2024-01-20 07:00:00', 'The minar was built by Qutbu\'d-Din Aibak in 1199 AD, with the purpose of being used as a mu\'azzin (crier) to give calls for prayer. His successor and son-in-law, Shamsu\'d-Din Iltutmish, added three more storeys to the minar during his reign from 1211 to 1236 AD. Each storey of the minar is adorned with a projected balcony supported by intricately designed stone brackets in a honey-comb pattern. This architectural masterpiece continues to stand tall and serve as a reminder of India\'s glorious past.', '2023122608064942e2dfe3d8c6b5cfe5bf0c43e477ac26.jpg', 'The Qutb-Minar, constructed in red and buff sandstone, is a towering monument and a symbol of Delhi\'s rich historical past. Standing at a height of 72.5 meters, it is the tallest tower in India, with a diameter of 14.32 meters at the base and about 2.75 meters at the top.', 'The minar was built by Qutbu\'d-Din Aibak in 1199 AD, with the purpose of being used as a mu\'azzin (crier) to give calls for prayer. His successor and son-in-law, Shamsu\'d-Din Iltutmish, added three more storeys to the minar during his reign from 1211 to 1236 AD. Each storey of the minar is adorned with a projected balcony supported by intricately designed stone brackets in a honey-comb pattern. This architectural masterpiece continues to stand tall and serve as a reminder of India\'s glorious past.', '20231226080649014b1f8ba98d486a7b2feb8b26584395.jpg', 'The best time to take photos is undoubtedly during the morning hours when the first rays of sunlight hit the sandstone walls, giving them a beautiful golden effect. This is the perfect time to embark on a Photowalk, as the monuments are at their most stunning and majestic state.', 'The golden light adds a magical touch to the already stunning sandstone walls, creating a picturesque landscape that is sure to take your breath away. These early hours also offer the perfect lighting for capturing intricate details and creating dynamic compositions. Whether you are a professional photographer or a beginner, the morning hours provide an excellent opportunity to capture the monuments in their full glory and showcase their grandeur through your lens.', 'What\'s also more interesting apart from the main structure are the nearby ruins. These ruins not only add to the overall aesthetic of the site, but they also provide insight into the history of the place. As one explores the area, they can see the remains of pillars and walls, which serve as a testament to the architectural skills of those who built them.', 'These nearby ruins offer a glimpse into the past and help paint a picture of what life would have been like in this place hundreds or even thousands of years ago. Moreover, for those interested in photography, this architectural site is a treasure trove of unique and captivating shots.', '20231226080650d8e352b05803fe4fc9863105254dca5d.jpg', 'The wide angle shots that can be captured from selected locations in the site allow for a more panoramic view and truly showcase the grandeur of the ruins. Overall, this is not just your average tourist attraction, but a place where one can immerse themselves in both the beauty and history of ancient architecture.', 'So, grab your camera and explore the beauty of these sandstone walls during the golden hour for an unforgettable Photowalk experience.\r\n\r\nParticipants need to pay the Gate pass Fee for entering Qutub Minar', '20231226080650206ff82aa33d1fe6f9aecc483d5c20b1.jpg', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '{\"1\":\"Participants need to pay the Gate pass Fee for entering Qutub Minar\",\"2\":\"Photowalk is open to all above the Age of 18 Years\",\"3\":\"Get to meet and interact with photography enthusiast and would love to join our photowalk community\",\"4\":\"Anyone interested in Photography and would like to spend morning weekends clicking and walking around the city\",\"5\":\"If you do not have a camera we will provide you with a mirrorless camera that will be shared with other participants during the photowalk. Please carry a SD Card to so you can take your clicked photos back. We would require a photo ID with address proof to be submitted at the time of the photowalk.\",\"6\":\"Please note that photo walks are done on foot, so expect lots of walking.\"}', '<div class=\"mapouter\"><div class=\"gmap_canvas\"><iframe src=\"https://maps.google.com/maps?q=Qutub%20Minar%20Ticket%20Centre&amp;t=&amp;z=13&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;iwloc=&amp;output=embed\" frameborder=\"0\" scrolling=\"no\" style=\"width: 100%; height: 600px;\"></iframe><style>.mapouter{position:relative;height:600px; 100%;background:#fff;} .maprouter a{color:#fff !important;position:absolute !important;top:0 !important;z-index:0 !important;}</style><a href=\"https://blooketjoin.org/blooket-host/\">blooket host</a><style>.gmap_canvas{overflow:hidden;height:600px;width: 100%}.gmap_canvas iframe{position:relative;z-index:2}</style></div></div>', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2023-12-26 15:06:50', '2023-12-26 17:50:01', NULL);
